      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "A solution to the linear equation $y=4x-11$ is the ordered pair $(2,h).$ What is the value of $h?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $(2,h)$ is a solution to the linear equation $y=4x-11,$ the equation must turn into a true statement if we substitute $2$ and $h$ for $x$ and $y.$ So, we replace $x$ with $2$ and $y$ with $h,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4x-11 \\\\ (h) & =4(2)-11 \\\\ h & =8-11 \\\\ h & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
